  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Convening Fund: UK-Nigeria TNE Capacity Building Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria&#x2019;s higher education sector faces a major challenge, with over 1.3 million qualified students unable to secure admission each year due to limited capacity. Transnational Education (TNE) partnerships between UK and Nigerian institutions offer a scalable solution by enabling students to access UK-accredited degrees locally, expanding access to quality education, and building a globally competitive workforce. Supported by the Science Granting Councils Initiative (SGCI), this programme will deliver a comprehensive TNE capacity-building framework through workshops, masterclasses, and knowledge-sharing activities. It aims to strengthen institutional capacity, transfer UK best practices, and support the implementation of Nigeria&#x2019;s TNE policy. Beneficiaries include Nigerian universities, UK partners, faculty, administrators, students, and regulatory bodies. Key deliverables include training materials, implementation guides, policy support documents, and a repository of best practices to ensure sustainable and impactful TNE partnerships.</narrative>
  </description>
